PRETABLE -- #530 (lcaisalane) kill table 3, CLOSING PASS 1's CLASS CLOSURE (77 rows).  Written BEFORE the table runs.
Instrument: regress/lca_isalane_probe.py, 77 rows = table 2's 51 + session 4d `cross' (12) + 4e `split67' (6) + four
split-head processes (8), frozen by the driver.  Measured before this file (table 1's binaries): FIX_r3.out 77/77,
HEAD_r3.out 49/77 -- the table-2 20 + the eight head rows.  *** HEAD_r3 MEASURES `lcaisaunaligned': a 1- or 2-byte head of
an UNALIGNED LDQ/STQ -- no BWX instruction -- ends the host on HEAD (h1/h2 ldq/stq alive rows), and the fix serves each
(h1 ldq 0x5a, h2 ldq 0x5a00, h1 stq 0x7e, h2 stq 0x96). ***

WHY: pass 2 and closing pass 1 found the same class -- a (len, lane, direction) cell of the position rule with no row --
one cell over each time (codex (8,0)R; grok (2,0), (8,0); minimax wide W at lane 1; glm wide W at lane 2; deepseek
len-6 heads; and the Opus closing seat MEASURED c1_w2, c1_w1w, c1_r4 at 51/51, each guest-visible).  Two passes, one
class: the repair rows the whole cross (probe header, THE CELL SPACE).

TARGETING: repair 2 ADDS sessions and changes no existing session's commands, so no earlier kill moves (the tables'
rule).  Table 3 therefore runs: base, head, the three measured escapes, and one mutant per closing-pass reading-seat shape.

CHECKS.  SIBLING PARITY: the store arm now carries every lane at len 1, 2, 4, 8 and every head length 1-7, as the read arm
does; the len-4 read at lanes 2/3 is rowed FULL-register (the witness's `ofs2/ofs3 wide' mask one lane).  CLAIM -> ROW:
the header's "any position other than (P & 3) % len, at every cell" maps to the cell space's rows.  CHANNEL (new rows):
full-register reads (a mis-filled other position differs) and flat readbacks of stores (the forwarded byte).

